From 28ae81ca9ea7ea189d8b17eb1afa5816457faf9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AK Sharma <maskachoska@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:53:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mediatek: filogic: fix MAC retrieval on JioRouter AX6000
 JIDU6801

The Telpa-built JIDU6801 reuses the jidu6101 DTS, so it lands in that board.d
case - but its u-boot-env MTD partition is a decoy and carries no 'mac' field
(the live env, a UBI volume, has none either). That left label_mac empty and
handed the empty string to macaddr_add(), which does

	$((0x${nic//:/} + val & 0xffffff))

i.e. $((0x + 1 & 0xffffff)). busybox ash rejects 0x as an arithmetic syntax
error, the subshell dies, and macaddr_add returns the literal ":" - which is
non-empty, so the [ -n "$lan_mac" ] guard downstream passes it through and
/etc/board.json ends up with "macaddr": ":". The box then ran on a random MAC
(fa:2e:85:96:db:78), changing every boot.

The factory MAC is the first 6 bytes of MFG: [redact-mac-0x27], which is the
WAN address and the LAN address - 1. That matches what stock programmed:
/etc/config/network on the unit has macaddr [redact-mac-0x27] on eth1 and
[redact-mac-0x28] on the lan interface, and its lan IPv6 link-local was
[redact-lladdr].

Read it only when the board is identified as a JIDU6801 by the model string in
MFG, because the MFG layout is not uniform across JioRouter AX6000 boards (the
6j01 branch reads 0x20 for JIDU6401 and an ASCII key at 0x1d0 for JIDU6601).
Nothing changes for a board whose u-boot-env does carry a mac, and if no MAC is
found at all the variables are simply left unset so the guards omit them rather
than writing garbage.

Verified: yields wan=[redact-mac-0x27] lan=[redact-mac-0x28] against the real
MFG dump, and the built rootfs contains the change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network   | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
index a289e10..4802a94 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -314,8 +314,23 @@ mediatek_setup_macs()
 		;;
 	jiorouter,ax6000-jidu6101)
 		label_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_ascii u-boot-env mac)
+		# The Telpa-built JIDU6801 shares this board's DTS but has no 'mac' in
+		# u-boot-env: that partition is a decoy there and the live env (a UBI
+		# volume) carries none either, which left label_mac empty and made
+		# macaddr_add below emit ':' plus "arithmetic syntax error". Its MAC is
+		# the first 6 bytes of MFG - the WAN address stock used, LAN being +1.
+		if [ -z "$label_mac" ]; then
+			local mfg_dev model
+			mfg_dev=$(find_mtd_chardev "MFG")
+			if [ -n "$mfg_dev" ]; then
+				model=$(dd if="$mfg_dev" bs=1024 count=1 2>/dev/null | strings |
+					grep -o -m1 'JIDU[0-9A-Z]*')
+				[ "$model" = "JIDU6801" ] &&
+					label_mac=$(get_mac_binary "$mfg_dev" 0x0)
+			fi
+		fi
 		wan_mac=$label_mac
-		lan_mac=$(macaddr_add "$label_mac" 1)
+		[ -n "$label_mac" ] && lan_mac=$(macaddr_add "$label_mac" 1)
 		;;
 	jiorouter,ax6000-jidu6j01)
 		local mfg_dev
